WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Read left to right from labeled CT to SimUS to SonoBridge at the same probe pose.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.700
The virtual probe samples the skin over the liver to choose a scan plane.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.850
The probe lowers until the central scanlines meet the skin.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.000
Two pulses illustrate incident, reflected and refracted rays.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.350
CT labels and simulated echoes share the same probe pose. SimUS uses display gamma 0.5.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.000
Purple marks vessels with V > 0.5, even in partial shadow.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.550
SimUS is on the left. The middle wipe reveals SonoBridge at the same probe pose.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:33.000
The moving scan on the right is an independent clinical training example. The two magnified regions are aligned.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.200
The image updates with the known probe pose.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.000
Axial rotation reveals a different liver plane.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.500
The reference stays at λ = 1 as vessel contrast fades and returns in the adjusted view.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.000
Same pose and λ = 1. Modeled shadow covers 36% of the sector before editing and 73% after.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Lowest distribution distances to clinical US on liver and kidney. Best anatomical match in 68% of blinded reader trials.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.500
Realistic ultrasound with aligned CT labels and known probe poses.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.000
